# song automation: EDIT held + a knob opens the slot screen - the parameter waits there until a white key
# places it on one of the song's four macros (a taken slot lights bright, a free one dim; the FX pages map
# their own effect's knobs); ALGO turns on the Song page cycle the slots' knobs
# and the four lane views; hold REC + turn the mapped knob while the song plays records it sixteenth by
# sixteenth, releasing REC stops the lane; a second pass overwrites the positions it touches; the song loop
# restarts the timeline; the save carries the lanes; SEL held + a knob clears one
# (a turn's third word is the detent's gap in ms: their comments never trail on the same lines)
wait 300
# a sixteenth is 125 ms at this tempo: the bars commands below count the steps
bpm 120
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
param 2 e1 20
tap EDIT
expect page Engine
# K1's parameter (e1) waits on the slot screen: white key 1 puts it on macro 1 - the screen lights a free
# slot dim, a taken one bright (leds: white ".+..." the first key dim, nothing placed yet)
press EDIT
turn K1 1
wait 60
leds
release EDIT
expect par2.e1 20
wait 60
tapkey w0
wait 60
# the mapping took the parameter, it did not touch its value
expect automap 1 2.e1 1
# the FX I page: EDIT + its K1 maps the effect's own knob (track 9) to macro 2, the second white key
tap FX
turn SELECT 2
expect page FX_I
press EDIT
turn K1 1
wait 60
leds
release EDIT
tapkey w1
wait 60
expect automap 2 9.e1 1
# a five-bar song loop: the automation's window outlives it, so the timeline wraps
song 1:1 1:1 2:1 3:1 1:1
songloop 1
tap HOME
expect page Arrange
turn SELECT 1
expect page Song
wait 60
# lane 1's curve under the slots
turn ALGO 1
wait 60
# the first pass: hold REC + the knob arms the lane, spinning it while held writes the curve
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
press REC
# the lane rests while it is being recorded: the knob has it
expect autoliv 1 -1
spin K1 6
bars 0.5
spin K1 6
bars 0.5
release REC
wait 60
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
wait 60
# every sixteenth of the pass is on the curve
expect auto 1 12
# the first spin's plateau, and the second's
expect autoval 1 1 3 26
expect autoval 1 1 11 32
# the stop cut the pass short: nothing past the recording
expect autoval 1 1 60 -1
# the stop gave the parameter back to the knob
expect autoliv 1 -1
# the lane's knob moved the parameter itself, live, and stayed there
expect par2.e1 32
# a second pass from the top: the positions it touches overwrite, the ones it does not keep the old curve
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
press REC
spin K1 -12
bars 0.75
release REC
wait 60
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
wait 60
# sixteenth 3 now holds this pass's value, not the old 26
expect autoval 1 1 3 20
# and sixteenth 14 keeps the first pass's 32: this pass never touched it
expect autoval 1 1 14 32
# the same positions: nothing new past either pass's end
expect auto 1 12
# and again the stop left the knob holding it
expect autoliv 1 -1
# plain playback: the curve drives the parameter, and a loop wrap restarts the timeline from sixteenth 1
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
bars 0.25
# the lane's second sixteenths, applied
expect autoliv 1 20
bars 5.5
expect autopos <32
expect playing 1
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
wait 60
# the stop gave it back to the knob
expect autoliv 1 -1
expect par2.e1 20
# and the save carries it all
projsave 1
reboot
wait 400
expect automap 1 2.e1 1
expect automap 2 9.e1 1
expect auto 1 12
expect autoval 1 1 3 20
expect autoval 1 1 14 32
# SEL held + a slot's knob: its mapping and its curve go, the parameter back to its knob for good
# Arrange, then the Song page again
tap HOME
turn SELECT 1
expect page Song
wait 60
# lane 1's view: its knob is the one SEL clears
turn ALGO 1
wait 60
press SEL
turn K1 1
release SEL
wait 60
expect auto 1 0
expect automap 1 2.e1 0
expect par2.e1 20
# macro 2's FX mapping goes the same way - unmapped, the effect's knob is never touched
press SEL
turn K2 1
release SEL
wait 60
expect automap 2 9.e1 0
